    "lines": [
      {
        "snippetId": "s6665",
        "messageOrdinal": 334,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-29",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "29 April 1846",
        "text": "Unless indeed she came out of that famous mist, which you fined me away into, ... the day you slew and idealized me, remember!—and, now I begin to consider, I think she did!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7454",
        "messageOrdinal": 372,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-25",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "25 May 1846",
        "text": "When you came yesterday I had scarcely done my grumbling over the Athenæum, which really seems to me to select its subjects from the things least likely to interest and elevate.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8122",
        "messageOrdinal": 401,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-06-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 June 1846",
        "text": "So, dear, dear Ba, understand and advise me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8167",
        "messageOrdinal": 403,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-06-13",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "13 June 1846",
        "text": "I will only say, I agree in all you write—it will be clearly best, and I can obviate every untowardness here ... show that all is pure kindness and provident caution ... so easy all will be!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9186",
        "messageOrdinal": 446,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-08",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "8 July 1846",
        "text": "Somebody is wanted to cut and burn, and be silent afterwards.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10261",
        "messageOrdinal": 487,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-08-05",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "5 August 1846",
        "text": "And you did understand also why I left, on that mere chance of danger to you,—for it was not, do you think it was only the irksomeness to myself I sought to escape—though that would have been considerable.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10462",
        "messageOrdinal": 493,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-08-10",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "10 August 1846",
        "text": "Thus it is.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10532",
        "messageOrdinal": 495,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-08-11",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "11 August 1846",
        "text": "And then came a note!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
